  "limits": [
    "Deep water only: the upstream solver is a deep-water free-surface kernel (nu = omega^2/g).",
    "Fixed body: the mission target is a body fixed in regular waves, so the mean drift force equals the added resistance; body motion (Pinkster's X.grad(dphi/dt) term) is not implemented.",
    "The near field needs the surface gradient of a piecewise-constant potential; the linear moving-least-squares recovery is first order in the panel size, so the near field converges to the far field only under mesh refinement.",
    "For ka < 0.3 the two estimators disagree by up to 34% because the drift force is a (ka)^3-small residual of much larger pressure and waterline terms.",
    "Chief-point choice of the upstream solver changes the result by ~50% at the coarse mesh; the default 'auto' chief points were used everywhere and the mesh ladder was run with them."
  ],
